PUBLIC RESPONSE: {A}

The trp attenuator relies on mutually exclusive RNA hairpin structures in the trpL leader transcript. The 3-4 hairpin (followed by the U-run) is the functional terminator. Under high tryptophan the ribosome translates through region 1 and physically sequesters region 2, freeing region 3 to pair with region 4 and form the terminator.  

A mutation that prevents region 1 from base-pairing with region 2 leaves region 2 free to pair with region 3 even when the ribosome is not stalled. Formation of the 2-3 antiterminator therefore sequesters region 3, blocking assembly of the 3-4 terminator. Transcription consequently reads through into the structural genes despite high tryptophan.  

Options B, C, and E either favor terminator formation or reduce transcription globally; option D has no direct effect on hairpin choice. Thus only A satisfies the stated phenotype.}

